A NOTE ON THE CHOICE, so it does not have to be made again

`therapeutic-studio-the-approach.md` proposes CC BY-NC-SA for the Other Bodies
tools and the resource library, and says to decide once. This is that decision,
applied here as well, for one reason: somebody else preparing for a counselling
master's in British Columbia should be able to take this structure and use it.
The verified facts in these notes are public facts that were tedious to gather,
and there is no reason for the next person to gather them again.

NonCommercial and ShareAlike are kept because the notes carry a standpoint and a
governing question, and neither should be repackaged and sold.

Note the deliberate contrast with Accessible Learning Labs, where
`the-studio-day-pattern.md` argues the licence should invert to CC BY or
CC BY-SA — because there, uptake is the evidence of impact and NonCommercial
gets in the way. That argument does not apply here. This repository is a working
reference, not a resource whose adoption is being measured.

This licence covers the contents of this repository only. It does not cover the
private record, which is not licensed to anyone and never will be.
